  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the other is labelled as Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.<br/><strong>Assertion (A)</strong> : Melting point of Boron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2453</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is unusually high in group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math> elements.<br/><strong>Reason (R)</strong> : Solid Boron has very strong crystalline lattice.<br/>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below ;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "X6hGW",
      "text": "Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) Is not the correct explanation of (A)",
